 ## [Unreleased]

+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates every tool call's `input` against the tool's declared JSON Schema
+  `inputSchema` before invoking the executor, compiling static schemas once at `register` time (throwing
+  synchronously if a schema cannot be compiled) and caching function-produced schemas by reference. Calls
+  that fail `required`, declared property `type` or `enum` checks return a `ToolResponse` describing the
+  failing field paths and constraints (without echoing or logging offending property values) instead of
+  throwing, so the model can self-correct within `maxToolRounds`; undeclared extra properties still pass
+  through unchanged without type coercion or injected defaults. **Migration:** executors that previously
+  hand-validated `input` now receive only arguments their `inputSchema` already accepts, and any tool that
+  relied on seeing malformed input to return its own custom error string will no longer be invoked on
+  schema-invalid calls.
+
